{{also|Handeln|Händeln}}
==German==

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|de|gmh|handeln}}, from {{inh|de|goh|hantalōn}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*handlōną}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|de|/ˈhandəln/|[ˈhandl̩n]}}
* {{audio|de|De-handeln.ogg|Audio}}
* {{hyphenation|de|han|deln}}

====Verb====
{{de-verb}}

# {{senseid|de|act}} {{lb|de|intransitive}} to [[act]]; to [[take action]]
#: {{ux|de|Jeder ist dafür verantwortlich, wie er '''handelt'''.|Everybody is responsible for the way they '''act'''.}}
#: {{ux|de|Wir müssen '''handeln''', bevor es zu spät ist.|We must '''take action''' before it is too late.}}
# {{lb|de|intransitive}} to [[negotiate]]; to [[bargain]]; to [[haggle]]
#: {{ux|de|Da lass ich nicht mit mir '''handeln'''.|I won’t '''bargain''' about this.}}
# {{lb|de|intransitive|_}} to [[trade]] in; to [[deal]]; to [[sell]] {{+preo|de|mit}}
#: {{uxi|de|Er '''handelt''' mit Teppichen.|He '''trades''' in carpets.}}
# {{lb|de|transitive|stock exchange|_|and the like}} to [[trade]]
#: {{ux|de|Eine Aktiengesellschaft ist eine Firma, die an der Börse '''gehandelt''' wird.|A stock company is an enterprise that is '''traded''' in the stock market.}}
#* {{quote-journal|de|year=2010|journal=w:Der Spiegel|url=http://www.spiegel.de/spiegel/print/index-2010-46.html|issue=46/2010|page=95
|passage=In Toronto '''werden''' mehr als 1400 Bergbaubetriebe '''gehandelt''', jede Woche kommen im Schnitt drei Unternehmen hinzu.|t=More than 1400 mining companies are traded in Toronto, three companies are added each week on average.}}
# {{lb|de|transitive|figurative}} to [[tip]] as; to take into consideration as being
#: {{ux|de|Er wird als der nächste Superstar '''gehandelt'''.|He’s being '''tipped''' as the next superstar.}}
# {{lb|de|intransitive|of a person|formal|literary}} to [[discuss]]; to [[deal]] with; to [[write]] or [[speak]] about {{+preo|de|von}}
#: {{ux|de|Der Autor '''handelt''' auf 32 Seiten von dieser Nebensächlichkeit.|The author '''discusses''' this marginal issue in 32 pages.}}
# {{lb|de|intransitive|with {{m|de||von}}|of a text, film, etc.}} to [[be]] about; to [[deal]] with
#: {{uxi|de|Das Buch '''handelt''' von Hasen.|The book '''is''' about hares.}}
# {{lb|de|impersonal|reflexive|often with {{m|de|bei}} to add clarification|idiomatic}} to [[be]], to be a [[case]] of, to be a [[matter]] of {{gloss|Often used to introduce the subject before giving it a name, or to indicate some uncertainty regarding exact amounts. Literally: it itself has to do with ...}} {{+preo|de|um}}
#: {{ux|de|Es '''handelt''' sich um ein Missverständnis.|What we have '''is''' a misunderstanding.}}
#: {{ux|de|Bei diesen Tieren '''handelt''' es sich um Hasen.|These animals here '''are''' hares.}}
#: {{ux|de|Es '''handelt''' sich um ein paar Tage, bis die Pakete ankommen werden.|It will '''be''' a matter of days before the packages will arrive.}}

